WSR 09-15-085

PERMANENT RULES

DEPARTMENT OF

SOCIAL AND HEALTH SERVICES (Economic Services Administration)

[ Filed July 14, 2009, 8:06 a.m. , effective August 14, 2009 ]

Effective Date of Rule: Thirty-one days after filing.

Purpose: The department is amending WAC 388-450-0015 What types of income does the department not use to figure out my benefits? Child support is currently a deduction from a household's countable gross income for Basic Food assistance. The department is exercising an option from the 2002 farm bill to treat child support payments made to someone outside of the home as an income exclusion prior to administering the gross income test.

Currently, some households are denied for Basic Food assistance for excess gross income, even when up to 50% of their income is paid out in child support. These families are now unable to qualify for food assistance due to income that they have no access to because it is paid out in child support. This change will enhance the division of child support's mission to collect child support and will enhance the community services division's mission to assist low-income families to access the Basic Food program.

Citation of Existing Rules Affected by this Order: Amending WAC 388-450-0015.

Statutory Authority for Adoption: RCW 74.04.005, 74.04.050, 74.04.055, 74.04.057, 74.04.510, and 74.08.090.

Other Authority: P.L. 107-171, section 4101.

Adopted under notice filed as WSR 09-12-117 on June 3, 2009.

